glitchlock invokes the FFglitch binaries (ffedit, ffgac) as external programs.
FFglitch is Copyright (C) 2018-2024 Ramiro Polla and is licensed under the GPL.
It is not linked into this project.

The MIT grant above covers the Python package, the web front end, the tests
and the documents. It does not cover ffglitch/: the patches there modify
FFglitch, which is FFmpeg, and each patched file keeps FFmpeg's LGPL-2.1+
header. Binaries produced by ffglitch/build.sh are configured with
--enable-gpl and are therefore GPL-2.0+; their complete corresponding source
is the ffglitch-0.10.2 tarball from ffglitch.org plus the patches in that
directory, in the order build.sh applies them.
